<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tulunid dynasty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">868–<a href="/years/905">905</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Tulunids</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Tulunid dynasty ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> from 868 to 905, the first dynasty to make Egypt effectively independent of the Abbasid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>. Its founder, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahmad-ibn-tulun">Ahmad ibn Tulun</a>, a Turkish officer sent as governor, built a new capital, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-qatai">al-Qata'i</a>, with the great <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mosque-of-ibn-tulun">Mosque of Ibn Tulun</a>. Abbasid forces reconquered Egypt in 905.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tulunid-dynasty.jpg" alt="Tulunid dynasty" width="320" height="229" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ro4444 · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tulunids_893.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
